1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:05,047
A checkout feature flag in Snowflake
is set to 25% in staging.

2
00:00:05,112 --> 00:00:06,755
What would change at 50%?

3
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:09,149
Start in the Developer app.

4
00:00:09,214 --> 00:00:11,024
Target new_checkout in staging.

5
00:00:11,089 --> 00:00:14,225
The update requires the current
value to be 25.

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:16,535
Run the update on a clone.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,883
One row goes from 25 to 50.

8
00:00:18,948 --> 00:00:20,633
The source stays at 25.

9
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:23,518
Send the request to a different reviewer.

10
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:25,910
They revalidate the change on current data,

11
00:00:25,975 --> 00:00:27,610
add a comment, and approve it.

12
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:30,434
Approval leaves the source untouched.

13
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:32,398
The reviewer confirms execution.

14
00:00:32,463 --> 00:00:34,916
Now the staging flag reads 50%.

15
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:38,863
The history shows who requested
and approved the change.

16
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:42,683
The execution query ID links the
decision to the update.
